# SynapseMemory — Local Development Environment
#
# This project has TWO env surfaces:
#   1. deploy/.env.example  → SINGLE SOURCE OF TRUTH for running the full stack
#      (engine auth, Postgres/pgvector, Redis, storage backend, demo-route gating).
#      Use this for `docker compose up` and any real deployment.
#   2. This file            → minimal local dev overrides only.
#
# For anything beyond a quick local spin-up, copy and edit deploy/.env.example:
#   cp deploy/.env.example deploy/.env
#
# ── Local dev quickstart (SQLite, no external services) ──────────────────────
# The engine runs fine with zero config locally: it uses SQLite, an auto-generated
# encryption key, and open dev auth. Set these only if you want to override that.

# Point the engine at a specific SQLite file instead of ./synapse_memory.db
# SYNAPSE_SQLITE_DB_PATH=./synapse_memory.db

# Provide an API key to require authentication even in local dev
# SYNAPSE_API_KEY=syn_live_your_dev_key

# Disable demo/simulated dashboard routes locally (on by default in dev)
# ENABLE_DEMO_ROUTES=false

# ── Optional LLM embedding provider ──────────────────────────────────────────
# SYNAPSE_EMBEDDING_PROVIDER=gemini
# GEMINI_API_KEY=
# OPENAI_API_KEY=

